          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/nodejs-22@22.22.1-r0?distro=dhi-3.23"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update nodejs-22 to 22.22.2-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-21715 is a Node.js Permission Model bypass: fs.realpathSync.native() did not check read permission, so code running under --permission with a restricted --allow-fs-read could test for and resolve paths outside its grant. Node.js fixed it for 22.x in 22.22.2, the 2026-03-24 security release (https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/march-2026-security-releases), with commit db48d9c675, 'permission: add permission check to realpath.native' (https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/db48d9c675), which carries this CVE id. Release notes: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v22.22.2. The CVE record (https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-21715) lists 22.x releases through 22.22.1 as affected. We read the node binary in every published DHI nodejs-22 package for Alpine 3.23 on x86_64 and aarch64: 22.22.2-r0 is the first that reports Node.js v22.22.2; 22.22.0-r0 and 22.22.1-r0 report Node.js 22.22.0 and 22.22.1. We also called fs.realpathSync.native('/etc/passwd') under --permission with a read grant for a different directory on the aarch64 builds: 22.22.0-r0 and 22.22.1-r0 resolve it, and 22.22.2-r0, 22.22.2-r1, 22.22.3-r0 and 22.23.5-r0 refuse it with ERR_ACCESS_DENIED. Both earlier builds predate the fix, so the range starts at 0."
    },
